\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 , US  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  as time was right - MOF source. \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1998\par 16:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the United States conducted joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market because the time was right, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) source said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "We have a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the time is right and not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the time is not right. And both we and the U.S. agreed that the time was right," the source said. \par \par \uc2  One reason the time was right was because the supplementary budget for fiscal 1999 was passed by parliament Wednesday afternoon, he added. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, Jiji news agency quoted MOF Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs as making similar remarks. \par \par \uc2  The decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  was taken following telephone conferences between U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin and MOF Minister Hikaru Matsunaga and a later conversation between Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto and U.S. President Bill Clinton on Wednesday, the source said. \par \par \uc2  "Both Japan and the U.S. were agreed that the achievement of a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and a strong yen are important," the source said. \par \par \uc2  Only the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  took part in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added, declining to comment further. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier confirmed to Reuters that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place in New York. \par \par \uc2  The source added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not necessarily to reverse a strong dollar trend. But he added that after a certain amount of time, some thought would also have to be given to a stronger yen. \par \par \uc2  He said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was important not only for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  but also for Asian countries whose stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been battered by the yen's relentless fall. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 8018 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6h02q0v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
