\par\par \b \uc2  Quick  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 , U.S. firms seen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  winners. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Alden Bentley \par \uc2 734 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1998\par 23:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, June 17 (Reuters) - Wednesday's round of joint American/Japanese dollar sales presents Japanese investors and U.S. corporations a great chance to reap a windfall from the cheaper dollar, if they act fast, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The surprise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gives Tokyo fund managers, recently liberated by financial deregulation, a window to boost purchases of dollars and U.S. financial assets while exiting Japanese markets at a better all-in level. \par \par \uc2  Japanese pension funds and other large investors in April were given greater leeway to invest in foreign-based assets, creating a massive capital exodus from Japan and contributing to the dollar's 12-percent rise this year. \par \par \uc2  Since April, many have found themselves chasing a rising dollar as they tried to acquire the greenback to settle purchases of U.S. securities. \par \par \uc2  April data released this week show net foreign purchases of foreign bonds jumped to record levels after Japan kicked off its "big bang" financial reforms that month and analysts see much more to come. \par \par \uc2  "They've been given an opportunity via big bang reforms to increase their percentage of exposures and they haven't really gone out and done that yet," said Jeremy Fand, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BankBoston. "There still could be a sea of money coming out of Japan that we have yet to see." \par \par \uc2  Beyond fundamentals, record low Japanese interest rates and the low credit quality of Japanese assets are a compelling reasons for Japan's portfolio strategists to boost weightings in foreign fixed income products. \par \par \uc2  In April, Fand said, the amount of net capital flowing from Japan into foreign bonds appeared exactly equal to the record amount of yen bought during \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's last bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , estimated at about $20 billion over the Easter holiday. \par \par \uc2  This implies that every time \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , domestic investors will jump at the chance to acquire offshore instruments more cheaply, he said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, as the dust settles, they may be joined by U.S. corporations who missed the boat on the dollar's recent rally. \par \par \uc2  American companies are contending with mounting Asia-related profit worries. Depreciated \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  mean lower foreign revenues when converted back to dollars, while the soaring greenback raises the price overseas consumers must pay for U.S.-made goods. \par \par \uc2  Many U.S. multinationals generate significant revenues in Asia. To satisfy internal policy requiring self-protection from translated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses, they may hedge by selling these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for dollars on a regular, often quarterly basis. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar selling could draw these players into the market and some \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  advisors are recommending that they hedge soon, predicting Japan will be unable to stop the yen rout for long. \par \par \uc2  "They'd like to take a day or two to digest it and figure out what's going on," said James Kemp, head of U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  "Some of them can hedge any time in the quarter, so they'll be interested in timing from that point-of-view. But typically they are fairly conservative in the way they manage \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk," he said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit fell six yen after the Federal Reserve and Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  blindsided the market by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Japanese unit in New York. Just one day earlier, the dollar hit a near eight-year high at 146.75 yen. \par \par \uc2  Fand said the coordinated action has presented U.S. companies with a great opportunity, adding that the dollar is very attractive between 137 and 135 yen. \par \par \uc2  "The biggest concern (some U.S. companies) have going forward is a runaway dollar and that they completely miss it and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  completely fall out of bed," Fand said. \par \par \uc2  "If Hong Kong and China devalue, that's clearly something that they didn't have on their radar screen a month ago ... if that's the case then they need to be hedging now." \par \par \uc2  Dealers predicted the yen rebound will not last, even if the authorities keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Japanese unit will get no lasting support until Tokyo presents a credible plan for economic growth, they said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's parliament on Wednesday implemented the supplementary budget for the 1998/99 fiscal year, which will finance part of the country's biggest ever stimulus package, first announced just before April's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((-N.A. \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit, 212 859 1667)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6h02paq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
