\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr under 144 yen at Tokyo noon after early rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 621 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1998\par 05:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0300 GMT\tab      TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT\par  USD/JPY     143.62/64\tab \tab    144.10-142.30\par  USD/DEM     1.7981/83\tab \tab    1.7992-1.7928\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, June 17 (Reuters) - The dollar was capped below 144 \par \par \uc2  yen by midday on Wednesday due to sporadic sales by Japanese \par \par \uc2  exporters and caution ahead of U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary \par \par \uc2  Lawrence Summers' expected visit to Japan this week. \par \par \uc2  Weak sentiment for the dollar that prevailed in early trade \par \par \uc2  was erased by brisk bargain-hunting by investors, falls in the \par \par \uc2  Indonesia rupiah and a loss of gains in Tokyo stocks. \par \par \uc2  "The news of Summers' visit to Japan has served as a deterrent for the dollar's rise," said a senior dealer at a U.S. bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, head of the International Finance Bureau of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told reporters on Wednesday that he had heard Summers would visit Japan, but that he did not know the schedule or expected topics of discussion. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun quoted U.S. government sources as saying Summers plans to have emergency meetings on Thursday with Japanese officials to discuss the yen's fall and shaky Asian markets. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said on Tuesday a decision on whether to send his deputy to Tokyo would be made shortly. News of Summers' trip to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised speculation over concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the yen's fall, but traders here were mixed about the main purpose of his visit. \par \par \uc2  "Discussions about concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be made over the phone," said a senior trader at a long-term credit bank. \par \par \uc2  "I think that the main purpose of his visit is to make Japan aware of the severity of Japan's economic situation and to urge it to take drastic steps (on economy and bad loans)," he added. \par \par \uc2  "If that is the case, there is a possibility that the dollar will resume its rise against the yen," he added. \par \par \uc2  Japan will tell U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers that it is doing its best to solve its bad loan problem, senior government spokesman Kanezo Muraoka told a news conference on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a European bank in Tokyo said given the fact that U.S. and Japanese monetary authorities apparently want to see the dollar ease at least below 140 yen to soothe other Asian nation's concerns about a weak yen, caution must be maintained during Summers' visit to Japan. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga said on Wednesday there has been no decision on whether the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "No decision has been made yet," he said. "I don't know if we will discuss it or not." \par \par \uc2  Uncertainty over whether Japan and the United States can hammer out effective measures to halt the yen's slide, however, encouraged investors to bargain-hunt for dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Investors who failed to buy enough dollars at lower levels are keen to buy dollars below 143 yen," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  There was talk that a medium-sized Japanese non-life insurance firm who had sold dollars on Tuesday stepped in to buy back dollars in early trade. This helped push the dollar up against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah recovered slightly to 16,200 against the dollar at 0305 GMT after touching a day low of 16,800, dealers in Jakarta said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 143.25/35 yen and 1.7980/90 marks in New York on Tuesday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 1396 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6h02p6o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
