\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Dollar Plunges Vs Yen But BOJ Not Seen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kenneth McCallum \par \uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 1998\par 07:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar fell sharply against the yen in Asian trading Tuesday, after traders, already nervous about the possibility of yen-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sold dollars in a panic amid widespread talk that overseas funds sold large amounts of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In a wild Asian session, the dollar initially surged to a new eight-year high of Y146.73, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's highest level since August 24, 1990, when it rose to Y146.75. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar plummeted nearly four yen from its intraday high amid widespread talk that U.S. and European funds had sold massive amounts of dollars for yen. The sales may have been options-related, and the dollar's drop may have been exacerbated by various stop-loss orders to sell the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Although there were vague and unsubstantiated market rumors that the BOJ sold dollars in the Singapore market, Tokyo dealers brushed them off as false. No dealer contacted by Dow Jones Newswires said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "It wasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ryohei Muramatsu, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Commerzbank in Tokyo. "Because the recent pace of the dollar's rise was very fast, it was just an adjustment." \par \par \uc2  The dollar later recovered some of its losses against the yen on bargain-hunting buying by short-term speculators and Japanese institutional investors, dealers said. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plunge against the yen also dragged the dollar about a pfennig lower against the Deutsche mark and pushed the mark down more than a yen to an intraday low of Y79.29. \par \par \uc2  Around 0530 GMT (1:30 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y144.80, below Y146.15 late Monday in New York and down from Y146.33 late Monday in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also was at DEM1.7995, lower than DEM1.8105 late Monday in New York and below DEM1.8137 in London Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 16-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0538GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6g0546h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
