\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar drifts down at Europe midday after shakeout. \b0\par\par\uc2 776 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 1998\par 12:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 16 (Reuters) - The dollar drifted below 145 yen after a sharp rebound from its overnight slide petered out in nervous European trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In a dramatic downmove, the dollar plunged four yen in Asian trade amid rumours of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Talk of a large sell order by an investment house and a correction from the dollar's rampant rise contributed to pushing dollar/yen to a low of 142.65 from levels above 146.50. \par \par \uc2  European trade lacked follow-through momentum though, capping gains here just below 146 and pushing the dollar to below 145 by midsession. \par \par \uc2  "We're in a period of nervous and exaggerated moves now," said Cameron Crise, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at SBC Warburg Dillon Read in London. "People are reticent to hold on to short-term positions because of the volatility, so there is a lot more two-way business rather than just yen selling." \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in the market, dealers were closely monitoring events in Russia as a recovery in markets there helped the mark to rebound. \par \par \uc2  At 0955 GMT the dollar was at 144.89/94 yen, up from an overnight low of 142.65 but down from 146.22/32 in late European trading on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 1.8004/09, up from a low of 1.7965 in Asian trading but lower than 1.8128/38 late here on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese officials had little marked impact on trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga said an extreme deviation of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates from economic fundamentals was unfavourable and he was "strongly concerned" about the yen. \par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami said he expected the economy to begin improving from late summer or early autumn but his comment that a rise in Japanese stocks and the yen could not be expected until the financial system stabilises was noted by yen bears. \par \par \uc2  Despite concern about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, dealers still do not believe Group of Seven \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is imminent. Overnight rumours of BOJ dollar selling were dismissed but dealers said the sharp reaction showed the high degree of nervousness. \par \par \uc2  "The fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to cause that sort of volatility," said Stuart Frost, strategist at NatWest. "There is going to be a lot of noise in the market ahead of 150 (yen), which is seen as a massive level," he told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the dollar rose sharply after U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only be a temporary tool and that the yen's weakness could only be remedied by stimulating Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  Its dire state was highlighted yet again by a 1.5 percent year-on-year drop in Tokyo department store sales and by downbeat comments in the Bank of Japan monthly report. \par \par \uc2  Today's figures follow last week's first quarter Japanese growth data which showed the world's second largest economy slid into recession. \par \par \uc2  The yen's weakness and Japan's failure to announce measures to tackle its financial crisis have provoked criticism from other Asian nations in recent days, while European and U.S. politicians and officials have also expressed their concern. \par \par \uc2  A spokesman for the Chinese government said the yuan will remain stable but called on Japan to take action to stop the slide of the yen, reiterating recent Chinese comments. \par \par \uc2  But as long as there is no sign from the U.S. administration that it is willing to change its strong dollar policy, dealers remain cautiously confident they can push the yen lower still, albeit at a slower pace, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan and other officials will testify from 1400 GMT before the Senate Judiciary Committee on mergers. Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer is also scheduled to speak on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the U.S. data front, dealers will be eyeing the release of U.S. consumer prices and housing permits for May at 1230 GMT and May industrial production/capacity utilisation at 1315 GMT, followed by earnings data at 1400 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Sterling jumped over a pfennig after higher than expected UK inflation data. Underlying inflation rose to 3.2 percent year-on-year from 3.0 in April, against forecasts for a rate of 2.9 and well above the government's target of 2.5. \par \par \uc2  The pound was at 2.9640/45 marks from 2.9637/42 in late Europe on Monday, while it traded at $1.6454/64 from $1.6339/49. \par \par \uc2  ((Astrid Zweynert, London newsroom, +44 171 542 7792, fax +44 542 52 93, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6g02ole\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
