\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Dollar Soars To Near 8-Year High Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kenneth McCallum \par \uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1998\par 08:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar continued its stellar climb against the yen in Asian trading Monday, breaking above Y145.00 and setting a near-eight year high, amid receding fears that there will be concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the yen's fall. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise to Y145.50 in late Asian trading triggered stop-loss orders to buy dollars, lifting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an intraday high of Y145.58. That was the dollar's highest level since August 24, 1990, when it rose to Y146.75. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that a whole range of market players, including Japanese institutional investors, importers, U.S. funds and Japanese banks, bought up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some Japanese investors bought dollars in order to acquire new dollar-denominated assets for Japan's semi-annual bonus season, while other players sold yen on renewed bearishness about the Japanese economy, as the country's stock prices continued to plunge. \par \par \uc2  But the biggest dollar-bullish factor was the growing speculation that the Bank of Japan won't be able to get the cooperation of other major central banks in defending the yen, dealers said. Some players see the dollar rising as high as Y150.00 in the next couple of weeks, though possible solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may temporarily slow the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. \par \par \uc2  "There is still some possibility that they will act," said Takashi Nakauchi, \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Manager at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. "But if it's the Bank of Japan acting alone, the impact will be limited, although it may slow the speed of the dollar's rise." \par \par \uc2  Around 0530 GMT (1:30 a.m. EDT), the dollar is quoted at Y145.45, above Y144.33 late Friday in New York and up from Y144.53 late Friday in London. \par \par \uc2  Against the Deutschemark the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at DEM1.8092, higher than DEM1.8061 late Friday in New York and above DEM1.8046 in London Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 15-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0600GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6f052vp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
