\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo -2: Dlr Hits Y145.00 On Nikkei Average's Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1998\par 03:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar lost a little ground in the wake of yen-supportive comments by officials from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But it soon rebounded to hit the Y145.00 mark for the first time since August 27, 1990, when it rose as high as Y145.55. \par \par \uc2  One trigger for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ascent was continued weakness in Japanese share prices, traders said. \par \par \uc2  After briefly falling below the 14,900 mark, the Nikkei average of 225 selected issue was down 92.61 points at 14,935.51 at 0135 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, head of the finance ministry's international finance bureau, said that Japan's partners from the Group of Seven nations share Japan's view that the yen's weakness is undesirable. He also said the G-7 nations are prepared to take steps on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as needed. \par \par \uc2  Despite the remarks, which hinted that there may be concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and its G-7 partners, dealers doubted that such action is actually in the works. \par \par \uc2  "Even if there is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it will be solo," said Nippon Trust Bank's Masumoto. \par \par \uc2  Tatsuya Ishii, senior sales manager at Banque Nationale de Paris, said the dollar may rise as high as Y145.45 for the remainder of Monday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be firmly supported at the intraday low of Y144.24, he added. \par \par \uc2  The mark is trading at Y80.24, up from Y80.08 earlier and above Y79.91 in New York late Friday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Friday at Y79.70. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6320, down from $1.6335 earlier and in New York late Friday. Sterling was at $1.6298 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is seen trading between Y144.20-Y145.45 and DEM1.8000-DEM1.8100 for the rest of the Asian day. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 15-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0139GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6f052n4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
