\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Dollar rises above 145 yen on Japan woes. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 575 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1998\par 06:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 15 (Reuters) - The dollar shot above the psychologically important 145 yen mark in Tokyo on Monday, the first full trading day after government data last week showed Japan to be in full recession. \par \par \uc2  It was the dollar's highest level since August 1990 and traders said there was little reason to buy the yen in the face of Japan's worsening economic conditions. \par \par \uc2  Active bids from interbank operators and commercial demand emerged from early in Tokyo trade, reflecting the dollar's bullish fundamentals, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 145.15/25 yen at 0300 GMT against 144.18/28 yen in late New York trade on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Without decisive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar should continue its upward journey," a senior Japanese bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The policy chief of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party sounded a warning against the yen's relentless selloff, saying a further fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  must be prevented, even if it meant joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks. \par \par \uc2  "The weak yen has a bad influence for Asia and so on, so we should prevent further drops of the yen even if it takes joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Taku Yamasaki told Reuters. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current account surplus data, a potential source of friction with overseas trading partners, provided policymakers with a rare moment of relief by showing a smaller-than-expected rise in April. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the country's broadest measure of trade in goods and services rose 10.3 percent in April from a year earlier to 1.17 trillion yen ($8.0 billion). \par \par \uc2  Economists said renewed turmoil in Asian economies dampened Japanese exports, while the recent weakness of the yen boosted import prices, suppressing the expansion of the surplus. \par \par \uc2  Despite the sliding yen and bad news on the economy, Tokyo stocks mostly held their ground. The benchmark Nikkei 225 average ended the morning down a modest 85.82 points, or 0.57 percent, at 14,936.51. \par \par \uc2  Brokers said sentiment was jarred by the yen's slide against the dollar and Friday's gross domestic product data showing the Japanese economy had slipped into recession. \par \par \uc2  But they said there were expectations in the market that Japan's cash-rich pension funds would launch rounds of buying, and this prevented any sharp fall in the Nikkei average. \par \par \uc2  "The GDP figures were weak...and I don't think the Nikkei 225 will head sharply higher any time soon," said Shinichi Ichikawa, a strategist at Credit Lyonnais Securities. But he added that the downside of the market was solid. \par \par \uc2  Data announced after the stock market closed on Friday showed Japan's GDP contracted at an annual rate of 5.3 percent in the January-to-March period against the previous quarter, its second consecutive quarter of negative growth. \par \par \uc2  Two quarters of GDP contraction is widely used as a definition of economic recession. \par \par \uc2  In debt markets, the key September JGB futures contract gained substantially by midday on Monday due mainly to short covering by foreign accounts, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The September ended the morning session at 133.95, up from 133.41 on Friday. The yield of the benchmark 182nd 10-year JGB was at 1.180 percent, down from 1.210 percent on Friday. ($1=145 yen) ((Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 8624 tokyo.newsroomzreuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6f0334q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
