\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  mkt breathes easier,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears ease. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 1998\par 20:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, June 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders breathed easier on Friday as many bet the world's most industrialised nations would not help Japan stem the yen's furiously fast fall before Tokyo institutes new reforms. \par \par \uc2  After the yen weakened further against the U.S. dollar on Thursday, falling to its lowest level since September 1990 when it hit 144.25 yen to the dollar, the market was braced for nervous trading, punctuated by rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It is Friday and rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  often circulate on Friday particularly as many dealers are heading out for the weekend," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market trader said. \par \par \uc2  But in early New York afternoon trading, dealers and analysts detected few signs of new nervousness about the possibility of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Of course the chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always possible, but I don't expect it and if it does occur, it will just give the market an opportunity to buy dollars back more cheaply," argued Peter Bruno, vice president at Generale Bank. \par \par \uc2  While analysts said the U.S. was clearly concerned that markets have punished Japan for its lack of forceful economic restructuring by sending the yen down nearly 17 percent since early February, the U.S. has little reason to sell dollars. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin underscored the Clinton administration's view on Thursday when he told the Senate's Finance Committee, "We are greatly concerned about the weakness of the yen. But the ultimate answer lies in the Japanese economy." \par \par \uc2  "The administration's mantra is clear, they do not want Japan to simply export its way to economic recovery, and other nations seem to agree," said Henry Willmore, senior economist at Barclays Capital. \par \par \uc2  Consequently, analysts took in stride Japanese Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga's statement that the agreement by the Group of Seven industrial powers to cooperate to prevent excessive declines in the yen was still in effect. \par \par \uc2  "The world is waiting for some real changes," Bruno said, referring to reforms in the Japanese tax and banking areas. \par \par \uc2  Analysts conceded there was a chance that the Bank of Japan would try to stem the yen's drop by catching the markets off-guard with a new round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "While it is possible that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  secretly wants a much softer yen, it seems a little odd, especially after they already spent a lot of money on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Willmore said. \par \par \uc2  Even if the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  were to try to surprise markets, dealers said the results would likely be lackluster. \par \par \uc2  In April, a last round of massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell short of desired results even though Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record $21 billion, or about 10 percent of its foreign reserves, to try to prop the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We really do not see much chance for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless there were some emotional rally to the 150 yen level," Bruno predicted. \par \par \uc2  Consequently, traders spoke of an unbroken interest in buying the dollars that Japanese investors need to find better returns elsewhere. \par \par \uc2  ((-NA Treasury Desk, 212-859-1638 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6c034gq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
