\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday -2: Taiwan  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\uc2 ; HK Dlr Dn \b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1998\par 05:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The decline in Taiwan stock prices was due partly to a fall in New Taiwan dollar. In response to the drop in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Taiwanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in early trading, pushing the Taiwanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to an intraday high of NT$34.510 against the dollar, dealers in Taipei said. The dollar is at $34.880 around 0230 GMT, lower than NT$34.896 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Hong Kong dollar also fell in the wake of a plunge in Hong Kong stocks. The U.S. dollar is quoted at HK$7.7477, up slightly from HK$7.7475 late Wednesday. The territory's benchmark Hang Seng index fell to its lowest level since February 1995 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has benefitted from receding expectations that Japan's Group of Seven nation partners would join \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in carrying out yen-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. They said that the lack of a statement after the G-7 deputies meeting Wednesday warning against the weak yen suggested that a G-7 joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not be in the works. \par \par \uc2  "The fact the the G-7 countries didn't issue any joint statement indicates they aren't willing to let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaken (against the yen), even though they may share Japan's concern over the weak yen," said Koichi Udagawa, assistant manager of the treasury and securities division at Daiwa Bank. \par \par \uc2  Another positive factor for the dollar was Wednesday's testimony by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan, who said the U.S. economy is in its best condition in 50 years and suggested the Fed won't raise interest rates in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Participants will keep an eye on a speech by Taku Yamasaki, a top policy maker at the ruling Liberal Democratic Party, scheduled for 0300 GMT, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The mark is at Y78.90, up from Y78.67 earlier in Tokyo and above Y78.80 in New York late Wednesday. The mark was quoted in Tokyo late Wednesday at Y79.11. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6287, down from $1.6391 earlier in Tokyo and below $1.6295 in New York late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.6370 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar is seen trading between Y142.20-Y140.90 and\par DEM1.7900-DEM1.8000 for the rest of the Asian day.\par    -By Sonoko Setaishi 813-5255-2933; ssetaishi@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 11-06-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0306GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6b050bj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
