\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/yen at new highs in Europe as Asia nerves grow. \b0\par\par\uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 09:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 10 (Reuters) - The dollar probed a fresh seven-year high against the yen in morning Europe amid growing nervousness over the economic situation in Japan and Asia. \par \par \uc2  The yen suffered a fresh bout of weakness amid concerns that China and Hong Kong will devalue if the yen continues to weaken, dragging down Asian stock markets and sparking a flight out of the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The indications that the yen slide is hurting China's economy is putting upward pressure on the dollar against the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which is feeding the move in dollar/yen," said Tim Fox, chief economist at Standard Chartered in London. \par \par \uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Dai Xianglong said Tuesday the depreciation of the yen was hurting China's imports, exports and foreign investment. \par \par \uc2  Although he noted previous promises not to devalue the yuan, markets took fright in that he did not explicitly rule out such a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's Hang Seng stock index fell to its lowest point this year alongside other regional stock markets. \par \par \uc2  Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also hit hard. The Aussie dollar hit a fresh 12-year low against the U.S. dollar and the Taiwanese dollar touched its lowest point in 11 years. \par \par \uc2  The yen won some respite in morning Europe amid signs that the Paris meeting of G7 deputy finance ministers touched on the dangers of the weak yen. U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said the G7 would continue to monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said dollar/yen over 140 was excessive and it will cooperate with other nations, taking measures as needed on the weak yen. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen slipped to 140.61/71 yen at 0810 GMT, down from its earlier seven-year peak of 141.55 yen but still just up from late Tuesday's 140.33/43 yen. Mark/yen also reversed its early gains, trading at 78.77/80 from a 79.18 yen peak earlier. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Summers' comments reinvigorated flagging expectations of co-ordinated G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen, but doubts that such action will take place as a result of the Paris meeting still remain. \par \par \uc2  "Rubin's comments overnight put the onus of turning the yen around squarely on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  still seems some way off," said a U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said late Tuesday the U.S. shared Japan's concern about the weak yen. He also said it was important that Japan get back to domestic-led growth and Japan's economic recovery was key to the revival of Asia. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Summers also said Wednesday the G7 had indicated its support for Russia and was willing to back further help through the IMF if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Market focus was also on the Bundesbank council meeting today amid ongoing speculation of a German interest rate rise. \par \par \uc2  "I think we'll see speculation of a rate hike surrounding every council meeting until the end of the year," said David Coleman, chief economist at CIBC Wood Gundy. "German rates will have to rise as the German economy picks up, but not just yet." \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank said it will not hold a news conference after today's meeting. \par \par \uc2  Attention was also on Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's testimony on monetary policy and the outlook for the U.S. economy before the Joint Economic Committee of Congress at 1500 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "The bias is for monetary tightening but Greenspan can't be too hawkish because of the effect on the world economy, he has to walk a very narrow tightrope," said Standard Chartered's Fox. ((Andrew Reierson, London newsroom +44 171 542 6745, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6a03aox\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
