\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/yen off highs amid renewed  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 13:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      LONDON, June 10 (Reuters) - The dollar stepped back from its earlier seven-year high against the yen in Europe amid renewed market expectations the G7 may yet step in to stem yen weakness. \par \par \uc2     U.S. Deputy Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers' comments earlier on Wednesday that senior officials of the G7 discussed the dangers of weak yen and would continue to monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates knocked the dollar below 141 yen in morning trade. \par \par \uc2     "The statements from Summers and the MOF indicate some concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is possible," said Klaus Kusber, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson. "The authorities look to be hinting they're prepared to do something about yen weakness." \par \par \uc2  Summers was speaking after a senior G7 officials' early meeting in \par \par \uc2  Paris before a G10 deputies session. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, Japan Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga said the dollar's rise above 140 yen was excessive and that Japan will cooperate with other nations on the weak yen, taking decisive measures when needed. \par \par \uc2  The comments saw the dollar retreat from an earlier peak of 141.55 yen, its highest level since June 1991, to trade at 140.63/73 at 1057 GMT. It stood at 140.33/43 late Tuesday in Europe. Mark/yen backed also backed away from a high of 79.18 down to 78.77/80 by midday European trade. \par \par \uc2  Analysts do not expect an official statement from G7 officials in Paris but are mindful of individual comments to reinforce the idea that the group of industrial nations sees the yen as being too weak. \par \par \uc2  "If their warnings lead to a breach of 139.75 yen support, then maybe the central banks will be more inclined to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and with the market in this case," said Dresdner's Kusber. \par \par \uc2  However, the gloomy economic outlook in Japan and Asia persists, the latest chapter being the growing concerns China and Hong Kong will be forced to devalue to combat the effects on its economy from the weakening yen. These concerns pushed Asia stock markets and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to new lows overnight. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said late Tuesday the U.S. shared Japan's concern over the weak yen, but added that it was key for Japan to get back to domestic-led growth. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers took this as an indication joint \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen will not be forthcoming until \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fundamental outlook improved. But concern that Asia will get worse before better is growing. \par \par \uc2  "It cannot be lost on world leaders that a show of support right now could go quite a long way to providing some confidence," said Tim Fox, chief economist at Standard Chartered Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, dollar/mark kept to relatively narrow ranges, but the tone was firm on general dollar demand from Asia weakness. \par \par \uc2  There was little impact from the Bundesbank's decision to hold its key rates steady, largely as expected but against an ongoing backdrop of expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise German interest rates by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark was trading at 1.7826/36 at midday Europe, off an earlier top of 1.7871 marks and just above 1.7812/17 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Summers' comments the G7 would back further help for Russia through the IMF gave some light support for the mark, said dealers. \par \par \uc2  Markets were also set to watch keenly Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's testimony on monetary policy and the outlook for the U.S. economy before the Joint Economic Committee of Congress at 1500 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Greenspan has to keep a careful balance between addressing the inflationary pressures of the U.S. economy against the impact that a hawkish bias towards U.S. monetary policy could have on the world economy and the Asia crisis in particular. \par \par \uc2  ((Andrew Reierson, London newsroom +44 171 542 6745, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6a03ajl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
