\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/yen capped as dealers eye BOJ,await G7 meeting. \b0\par\par\uc2 691 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 1998\par 13:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 8 (Reuters) - The dollar was capped close to its highs against the yen at midsession in Europe on Monday after fading expectations of Group of Seven yen support jolted the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a seven-year high. \par \par \uc2  The market cooled off and adopted a wait-and-see attitude ahead of the U.S. open and Tuesday's meeting of Group of Seven (G7) deputy finance ministers in Paris. \par \par \uc2  With the psychologically important 140 level now broken, market concern about the possibility of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The speed of the yen decline is striking - and it has made the market cautious about BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Georgio Radaelli, head of European market research at First Chicago in London. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen has surged by about 6.7 percent in the past month. At 1050 GMT the dollar was at 140.28/38 yen, up about half a percent from 139.64/74 in late Europe on Friday, and down from 140.73, its highest level since June 1991. \par \par \uc2  Against the mark, the dollar was little changed at 1.7750/60, while mark/yen hovered around 79 yen, off a peak at 79.20, the highest since December 1992 and up from 78.71/74 late in Europe on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "With Japan insisting that the weaker yen would not be a topic in tomorrow's G7 meeting, the strategy would be to be continuing buying the dollar on dips against most of the region's units," said Mitul Kotecha, economist at Standard Chartered. \par \par \uc2  Just how nervy the market is about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was highlighted on Friday when rumours that the BOJ had been checking rates aggressively on Friday sent dollar/yen plunging by well over a yen. \par \par \uc2  The impact of the yen's latest slide on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased market concern about contagion in the region as regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  eyed key psychological levels. \par \par \uc2  A major worry for policymakers is that China might have to resort to devaluation and Hong Kong might sever its peg to the U.S. dollar as both countries fend off the competitive pressures of a weak yen, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Singapore Senior Minister Lee Kuan Yew said on Saturday further yen falls against the dollar could pressure China to eventually devalue the yuan. He said China would be able to defend the yuan for at least a year but that levels such as 150, 160, 170 to the dollar would be difficult for China. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to a European session low of 140.10 yen after Koji Tanami, vice minister at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Japan must consider the effect of the yen's fervention is questionable. BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last April to the tune of $20 billion failed to stem the yen's slide. \par \par \uc2  Despite a surge in Japan's trade surplus of 933.3 percent year-on-year in the first 20 days of May, analysts said it was unlikely the U.S. would change its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  Even though the firm dollar makes U.S. exports dearer, the world's largest economy is still going strong, as highlighted by a 296,000 rise in non-farm payrolls in May. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark was likely to remain stuck though around current levels unless dollar/yen surged further, dealers said. The prospect of a strong German jobs figure this week has given the mark support. Chancellor Helmut Kohl said last week the jobless number would fall by about 200,000 to 4.2 million on an unadjusted basis. \par \par \uc2  The yen's slide pushed the Australian dollar below US$0.6000 for the first time in 12 years. \par \par \uc2  The Bank for International Settlement's annual report indicated the dollar was noticeably overvalued against the mark and the yen when looking at the widening U.S. current account deficit and the external debt. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was also on hold ahead of testimony by Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (London newsroom, +44 171 542 7792, fax +44 542 52 93, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6803hrx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
