\par\par \b \uc2  TOCOM precious metal futures end mixed. \b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 1998\par 09:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 8 (Reuters) - Yen-based Tokyo precious metal futures ended mixed on Monday as early buying interest reflecting the dollar's gains against the yen lost steam late in the day, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Weak spot gold prices prompted gold futures to weaken by the close, they said. \par \par \uc2  Uncertainty over how much gold the European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold in its reserves kept private investors wary of building large fresh positions. \par \par \uc2  Nearby palladium contracts ended higher as traders failed to sight signs that long-awaited talks between Japan and Russia on 1998 supplies have started. \par \par \uc2  Gold futures ranged from flat to one yen per gram lower. Benchmark April finished down one yen at 1,298 yen. \par \par \uc2  In the bullion market, spot gold was quoted at $289.25/75 per ounce at 0718 GMT, against $291.40/90 in New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Bullion was weak during Asian hours due partly to selling, believed to be from Australian producers taking advantage of weaker local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," an analyst at a commodity broker said. \par \par \uc2  A widespread view that the dollar may fall against the yen due to possible attempts by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the yen, also limited trading interest in gold futures, they said. \par \par \uc2  Trading in palladium futures was directionless. \par \par \uc2  "We saw some short-covering in nearby months, while private investors were wary of building fresh longs in distant months due to a perception that palladium prices have reached their near-term ceiling," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Russia's platinum group metal agency, Almazjuvelirexport, has not yet informed Japanese customers when they will start supply contract talks for this year. \par \par \uc2  Palladium futures ranged from five yen per gram lower to 16 yen higher. Benchmark April was up four yen at 1,136 yen. \par \par \uc2  Silver futures ended firmer in line with stronger spot silver prices. Prices ranged from 1.4 yen to 5.7 yen per 10 grams higher. \par \par \uc2  Platinum futures ranged from seven yen per gram lower to eight yen higher. Benchmark April ended down two yen at 1,544 yen. ((Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 7431 tokyo.commodit.newsroom @reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6803dln\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
