\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday -2: G-7 Deputies Seen Not Discussing Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1998\par 05:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  As for the G-7 deputy meeting, many market participants said they are now skeptical that the dollar-yen rate will be discussed at the G-7 meeting. Kyodo News Service on Thursday quoted an unnamed Japanese Finance Ministry source as saying \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't on the agenda. \par \par \uc2  Even so, "some are cautious that the U.S. and Japan may, for instance, issue a joint statement cautioning against the weak yen," said a Japanese city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  But fears that other G-7 nations may join force with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the yen appear to be abating, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The Asian situation isn't bad enough for the U.S. to take action," said Shuji Takano, assistant manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ABN-Amro Bank N.V. "European countries are even more reluctant, because they aren't feeling the impact of Asia," he said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, traders said the mark will remain well bid against the yen Friday after the release of robust German first-quarter gross domestic product data on Thursday. Signs that Russia's financial markets are stabilizing, after the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its benchmark rates to 60% from 150% Thursday, have also boosted mark bullishness. \par \par \uc2  "Both U.S. funds and Japanese investors bought the mark for yen," said a Japanese bank dealer. "The trend is European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are a buy and the yen is a sell," said another Japanese city bank dealer, adding that the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to move between Y78.10 and Y78.60 for the rest of Friday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is at Y78.48, up slightly from Y78.46 earlier in Tokyo and above Y78.29 in New York late Thursday. The mark was quoted in Tokyo late Thursday at Y78.08. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6360, up from $1.6353 earlier in Tokyo but below $1.6367 in New York late Thursday. Sterling was at $1.6390 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 05-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0304GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6504tco\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
