\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Tokyo Volatilities Dn As Spot Mkt In Range \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 1998\par 06:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--With the dollar poised to go above Y139.00 but temporarily stuck in a narrow range in the spot market, volatilities implied by yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options have eased a bit Monday from levels late Friday in New York. Deutschemark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options are lower as well. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has traded between Y138.50-138.85 during the Asian day, as profit-taking on the upside has hindered the dollar's advance. While market participants seem confident that the dollar will soon break through resistance and try for Y140, the lack of news on which to trade is keeping volatilities muted. \par \par \uc2  "Volatilities are basically unchanged from Friday because there's not a whole lot happening," said an options trader at a Japanese bank. "Of course, with Y140 well within sight, it's hard to sell yen volatilities off, but they aren't moving up now either." \par \par \uc2  The market remains cautious but calm over the prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen. Risk-reversals continue to favor dollar put options against the yen as investors hedge their bets over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen having little more than a short-term impact. \par \par \uc2  Risk-reversals measure the market preference for either put or call options by the premium or discount applied. \par \par \uc2  In the over-the-counter market, one-month at-the-money dollar/yen options imply volatility of 12.8% bid, just below 12.85% in New York Friday, but above 12.7% in Tokyo Friday. Against the mark, they are lower at 8.8% from 9.0% in New York Friday. Dollar/mark options were quoted at 9.3% in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0415 GMT (12:15 a.m. EDT), the dollar is at Y138.85 and DEM1.7840,\par slightly down from Y138.91 and DEM1.7858 late Friday in New York.\par By John Brinsley; 813-5255-2929; jbrinsley@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-06-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0427GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1077 4127 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6104nno\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
