\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup -2: BOJ Action Possible, But Limited \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 1998\par 08:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The dollar's path to Y140 is mitigated by more option-related selling around Y139.40-Y139.50 as well as lingering fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  But given that many economists see Japan entering a deflationary spiral, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may find it in the uncomfortable position of defending an indefensible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And the U.S. is not likely to help, given that dollar-selling by the Treasury could spark panic selling on Wall Street. \par \par \uc2  "Of course \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this level wouldn't be surprising, but there's a question as to whether it would be good policy," Asahi Bank's Takane said. "Any action would be unilateral and therefore temporary. The dollar might go down into the Y137 range for a bit, and then come back. The BOJ would be throwing its money away." \par \par \uc2  The fall in the Nikkei was in part fueled by a rumor that Nissan Motor Co. had suffered a huge derivatives-related loss. A Nissan spokesman called the rumor "baseless," but the Nikkei was down 269.88 points at 15,400.90 at 0550 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "If the Nikkei ends more than 300 points down, you're going to see the dollar rise in London and New York," Takane said. However, other dealers said that momentum might be hindered by the lack of liquidity in Europe, as several countries are on holiday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise against the yen was helped by the mark's rise above Y78 late in Tokyo trading. \par \par \uc2  "After falling on profit-taking last week, the mark has rebounded against the yen," the Japanese bank trader said. "Continued demand for marks is going to help dollar-yen." \par \par \uc2  The mark is quoted at Y78.01, up from Y77.79 in New York late Friday and above Y77.63 in London late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6290, down from $1.6323 in New York late Friday. Sterling was at $1.6330 in London late Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By John Brinsley; 813-5255-2929; jbrinsley@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0608GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6104ne1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
