\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr steady vs yen Tokyo midday,lacks fresh factors. \b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 1998\par 05:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0318 GMT\tab      TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT\par  USD/JPY     138.72/75\tab \tab    138.82-138.44\par  USD/DEM     1.7840/45\tab \tab    1.7850-1.7811\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, June 1 (Reuters) - The dollar was steady versus the \par \par \uc2  yen at midday on Monday after its early downside test found a \par \par \uc2  solid floor at around 138.50 yen. \par \par \uc2      Dollar/yen was range-bound below 139 yen by late morning \par \par \uc2  due to a lack of fresh market factors, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      "The dollar lacks direction because there are no fresh \par \par \uc2  market factors," said a senior dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar came under pressure against the yen in early Tokyo trade after it hit 139.25 yen in London on Friday, its highest level since August 1991. \par \par \uc2  Yen buying was also fueled by news over the weekend of a possible business tie-up between Japanese and U.S. financial firms, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Nikko Securities Co Ltd  confirmed at the weekend that it and Travelers Group Inc of the United States  had been in negotiations on a possible tie-up. Nikko said on Monday that it and Travelers plan to hold a joint news conference later in the day. \par \par \uc2  But the greenback quickly bounced back as buying interest from Japanese institutional investors was detected at around 138.50 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar fell against the yen in early trade, partly on the news about Nikko Securities, but the falls were limited as buying emerged from some other trust banks," said the trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Commercial dollar demand ahead of the local fixing at 0100 GMT also provided support for the dollar, he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said domestic and external factors continued to weigh on the yen. \par \par \uc2  Concern remained about Japan's economy after the government announced on Friday that the unemployment rate had surged to a record 4.1 percent in April from 3.9 percent in March. \par \par \uc2  "Looking abroad, the market is worried about India-Pakistan tension and the financial turmoil in Russia. There simply isn't a good reason to buy the yen," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's rise was limited for now amid a lack of fresh market factors, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Corrective selling of the mark against the yen also indirectly weighed on the dollar/yen, they said. Mark offers were detected by U.S. fund operators at around 77.80 yen. \par \par \uc2  The mark was at 77.75/78 yen at 0350 GMT versus about 77.70 yen in late New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The market shrugged off comments over the yen by a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official on Monday morning, but caution remained about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's test at 140 yen may trigger a wave of technical selling. That might give a chance for the Japanese authorities to step in," the trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  MOF's Haruhiko Kuroda told reporters on Monday Japan is concerned about the excessive weakness of the yen. He also said that the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy remained unchanged. ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3 3432-8570 fax +81-3 3432-7462, tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6104174\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
