\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr off lows in early Tokyo,supported by investors. \b0\par\par\uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 1998\par 02:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, June 1 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0009 GMT -- \par \par \uc2      *Dollar off earlier lows versus yen in early Tokyo on \par \par \uc2  Monday, after erasing losses on buying by U.S. fund operators. \par \par \uc2      *Earlier, dollar slipped as low as 138.44 yen, as selling \par \par \uc2  of mark versus yen indirectly weighed on dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2      *But greenback quickly bounced back as buying interest from \par \par \uc2  Japanese institutional investors was detected above 138 yen, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2      *Dollar/yen at 138.73/78, compared with 138.75/80 in New \par \par \uc2  York on late Friday. \par \par \uc2  *Domestic and external factors continue to weigh on yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *"Concerns about Japan's economic fundamentals actually mounted last week after a jump in the jobless rate," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  *Japan's unemployment rate surged to a record 4.1 percent in April from 3.9 percent in March, the government said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  *"Looking abroad, the market is worried about India-Pakistan tension and financial turmoil in Russia. There simply isn't any good reason to buy the yen," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  *But some dealers said they expected to see a correction in the dollar/yen this week after dollar's three-yen rally last week. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar hit 139.25 yen in London on Friday, its highest level since August 1991. \par \par \uc2  *"I am cautious about chasing up dollars from here, as the dollar could come under pressure if U.S. jobs data due out on Friday shows inflationary threats," said a dealer at another city bank. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers also said market remained cautious about possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  *Haruhiko Kuroda, director-general of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (MOF's) International Finance Bureau, told reporters on Monday MOF was concerned about excessive weakness of yen. \par \par \uc2  *He also said Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was unchanged. \par \par \uc2  *"Profit-taking interest is likely to be quite strong above 139 yen. Options-related offers are also expected to emerge when the dollar rises closer to 140 yen," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  *There is talk of knockout options positions with strike prices set around 140 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  2303 GMT - *Dollar slightly down versus yen in early Asia on Monday, but seen well supported by number of factors such as uncertainties in Russia and tension in South Asia. \par \par \uc2  *"The dollar should remain strong this week as there is plenty of bullish news for it," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar was at 1.7819/24 marks, compared with 1.7855/65 marks in New York on late Friday. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar rose versus mark on Friday after Moody's Investors Service announced a cut in Russia's country ceiling for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds and notes to Ba3 and the country ceiling for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank deposits to B1. \par \par \uc2  *United States said on Sunday it would help mobilise more aid for Russia if needed from international financial institutions to calm Russia's financial markets. \par \par \uc2  *Tension in South Asia after Pakistan conducted another nuclear test on Saturday is expected to help keep dollar well supported, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *But lack of potentially market-moving events is likely to keep dollar/yen and dollar/mark rangebound in Asia on Monday, dealers said. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du61040zi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
