\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Treasurys In Tokyo Narrowly Mixed Midday; 30-Yr -2/32 \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 1998\par 04:34\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Prices of U.S. Treasurys in Tokyo are\par narrowly mixed Friday in very quiet trading as local players\par nervously adjust their positions ahead of the long weekend,\par traders said.\par    A rumor overnight in New York that the Bank of Japan sold\par Treasury bills has fueled persistent rumors that\par yen-supportive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets by\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday's U.S. holiday is possible,\par traders said.\par    Not even the stronger yen against the dollar has been\par able to entice buyers this session, traders said. The dollar\par was at an almost seven-year high against the yen on Tuesday.\par    5 5/8%   2-year 100  1/32   Up  1/32  5.61%\par    5 3/4%   5-year 100 15/32   Up  1/32  5.64%\par    5 5/8%  10-year  99 24/32   Dn  1/32  5.66%\par    6 1/8%  30-year 102 24/32   Dn  2/32  5.93%\par    2-to-30-Year Yield Spread: 32 BPS Vs 30 BPS\par    At the Chicago Board of Trade, the June bond futures\par contract recently traded at 120-15, unchanged from the\par previous close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Meanwhile the June Eurodollar contract on the\par Singapore International Monetary Exchange recently traded at\par 94.285, down from the previous close of 94.290.\par    The transfer of power Thursday from Indonesian President\par Suharto to Bacharuddin Jusuf Habibie, a close Suharto ally\par and his former vice president, had very little effect on\par Treasurys prices, but boosted the yen against the dollar,\par traders said.\par    "It doesn't mean Indonesia's economy is recovering," said\par a trader at a Japanese securities firm. Traders said that as\par far as Treasurys market participants are concerned, little\par has changed in Indonesia.\par    The dollar recently traded at Y135.33, up from Y134.95 in\par New York late Thursday but below Y135.62 late Thursday in\par Tokyo.\par    -By Karen Hawkins; 813-5255-2939, khawkins@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  05-21-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2234EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1079 4041 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du5m01akh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
