\par\par \b \uc2  Yen Cross - Mark higher in Tokyo as dlr/mark capped. \b0\par\par\uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 1998\par 06:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 20 (Reuters) - The German mark posted healthy gains against the yen in early afternoon cross trade on Wednesday due to persistent buying by U.S. fund operators. \par \par \uc2  A senior dealer at a European bank said that a major U.S. fund operator had been buying mark/yen in recent days. \par \par \uc2  "The next target (in the mark/yen) would be at 77.25 yen as the dollar now looks top-heavy against the mark. The dollar's fall through a support point of 1.7805 marks gave us a good reason to buy up the mark/yen," he said. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo operators are more at ease buying mark/yen than dollar/yen due to concern over possible dollar selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), dealers said. This is another factor supporting the German unit, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the mark rallied to around 76.70 yen by late morning trade on Wednesday, its highest since February 1993. \par \par \uc2  The mark/yen also gained momentum because Japanese exporters were refraining from selling for now, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We saw exporters placing offers at 76.80-90 yen yesterday. But they withdrew these offers this morning," said a dealer at a long-term credit bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was a trigger point of options-related buying at 77.25 yen. If triggered, that may pave the way for the mark to rise to 80 yen, they said. \par \par \uc2  "There is heavy Japanese demand to sell yen toward the month-end," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  New foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated investment trusts are expected to be set up around the end of May, while Japanese institutional investors are showing strong interest in European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they are eagar to shift part of their portfolios away from U.S. dollars, he said. \par \par \uc2  "Since trade in the dollar/yen withered due to fears of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trade in yen crosses has heated up," he added. \par \par \uc2  The German mark was at 76.72/75 yen at 0306 GMT against around 76.49 yen in late New York on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar fell to 1.7780/85 mark at 0312 GMT versus New York's 1.7834/39. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's brief recovery against the mark ended overnight after the U.S. Federal Reserve kept interest rates steady on Tuesday and a member of Germany's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped fan speculation the Bundesbank may soon consider raising rates. \par \par \uc2  Ernst Welteke, a member of the Bundesbank's policy-setting council, rekindled speculation that Germany may mull another rate hike as the nation prepares for European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  union in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  "I cannot rule out a slight interest rate hike, but it is too early to speculate when," Welteke told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Swiss franc was at 92.54/59 yen at 0335 GMT versus 92.21 yen in late New York on Tuesday, while sterling was at 221.87/99 yen versus New York's 221.22. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said Japanese investors had recently been keen to buy the ecu, and partly because of such buying, the ecu rose above psychological resistance at 150 yen earlier this week. The ecu was at 151.35/40 yen at 0338 GMT on Wednesday. ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3 3432-8570 fax +81-3 3432-7462, tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5k04z7u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
