\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar steady vs yen in Tokyo, focus on Indonesia. \b0\par\par\uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 1998\par 02:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, May 20 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0025 GMT -- *Dollar steady versus yen after earlier \par \par \uc2  rises checked by selling in relation to report on Indonesia. \par \par \uc2      *Dollar at 136.28/33 yen vs New York at 136.38/48. \par \par \uc2      *Amien Rais, leader of nation's second-largest Moslem party, \par \par \uc2  called off plans for mass "people power" demonstration, \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's official Antara news agency reported on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      *But not clear whether thousands of students who also plan \par \par \uc2  to take to streets would also abandon their protests. \par \par \uc2      *Selling from U.S. fund operators also detected in Sydney, \par \par \uc2  mainly seen as profit-taking, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *Some said Japan's larger-than-expected trade surplus for April, released at 2350 GMT, also capped dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  *"The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market reacted slightly to the data. But it should have a longer-term impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, rather than on today's sentiment," said a senior dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  *Japan's trade surplus rose 52.6 percent in April from year earlier to 1.23 trillion yen on customs-cleared basis, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. Economists polled by Reuters had estimated surplus ranging from 1.014 to 1.207 trillion in April. \par \par \uc2  *Surplus with the United States rose 29.2 percent to 585.98 billion yen in April, MOF said. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar rose to 136.50 yen in early Asia on expectations of Japanese buying for setting fresh investment trusts. Lack of offers from exporters means dollar's momentum intact. \par \par \uc2  *"Offers by exporters at 136.70-80 yen were traded in New York, albeit in a small volume," said a dealer at a long-term credit bank. But offers were withdrawn by Wednesday morning either in dollar/yen or in cross yen trade, he said. \par \par \uc2  *Dealers said despite early correction, dollar may follow uptrend with some expecting to test new 6-1/2-year high above 136.80 yen in Tokyo. Indonesia uncertainty and weak business results of Japanese firms due this week positive for dollar. \par \par \uc2  *Some dealers said large-lot knock-out options rumoured at 137 yen. A break above that level may trigger short-covering, resulting dollar's rise to 137.50-138.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  2309 GMT - \par \par \uc2  *Dollar firmer versus yen in early Asia after upside test overnight ended at 136.80 yen, level market had considered a technical resistance point. \par \par \uc2  *Focus on Indonesia, where nationwide protests against President Suharto scheduled for Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  *Caution lingers over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *"Because of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears, dollar bulls are quick to square off their long positions. But if today's demonstrations turn into new rioting, the dollar may rise above 136.80 yen," said a dealer at a long-term credit bank. \par \par \uc2  *On Tuesday, U.S. Federal Reserve kept interest rates steady, as expected. \par \par \uc2  *In New York on Tuesday, dollar rose to a fresh 6-1/2-year high against yen, but fell against mark after Ernst Welteke, a member of the Bundesbank's policy-setting council, rekindled speculation that Germany may mull another rate hike as the nation prepares for European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  union in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  *"I cannot rule out a slight interest rate hike, but it is too early to speculate when," Welteke told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar followed overnight falls versus mark in early Asia. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar at 1.7790/95 mark at 2340 GMT versus 1.7834/39 in New York. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar/mark also under pressure from firmness in mark/yen as Tokyo operators find buying easier in mark/yen than in dollar/yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *Decisive break below 1.78 mark could target 1.7720 area, although support expected at around 1.7770, they said. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3 3432-8570 fax +81-3 3432-7462, tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5k04ys5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
