\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar seen testing Y140 on Japan economy,Jakarta. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 1998\par 09:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 19 (Reuters) - Political uncertainty in Indonesia and concerns over Japan's economy have set the scene for a further attack on the yen, with dealers predicting that it could weaken to 140 yen against the dollar in the near term. \par \par \uc2  As the dollar broke through this year's high of 135.45 yen on Monday, the market has turned increasingly confident about the outlook for the greenback, dealers said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "It now appears we're more likely to see the dollar heading up towards 140 yen after breaking through this year's high (in New York on Monday)," said Hidenori Omori, senior manager of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets section at Norinchukin Bank. \par \par \uc2  While fears over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) still exist, dealers said even \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action is unlikely to alter the basic bullish trend of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Ample evidence of the weakness of the Japanese economy and no clear signs of recovery have put pressure on the yields of Japanese government bonds, sending them down to record lows. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the benchmark 182nd JGB fell to a record low of 1.240 percent in Tokyo on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In addition to domestic economic problems, widespread turmoil in Indonesia has recently depressed Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the dollar briefly came off its high against the yen due to comments from Indonesian President Suharto in a nationwide televised address. \par \par \uc2  Suharto promised new elections as soon as possible and said he would not stand in them. \par \par \uc2  "The market has tended to use the possible resignation of Suharto as a factor to buy the yen recently, but such buying should only be temporary," said Noriyuki Mizukami, head of treasury sales at National Westminster Bank (NatWest). \par \par \uc2  One senior dealer at a Japanese city bank said that even though the market bought back the yen after Suharto promised to step down, tension in Indonesia had not eased. \par \par \uc2  "There are still many uncertainties even if Suharto quits. I don't believe the market will continue buying the yen on Suharto's resignation alone," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar-buying interest from the Japanese was still strong with many domestic institutional investors and private investors eager for a chance to buy high-yielding foreign investments. \par \par \uc2  "There is substantial dollar buying demand from investors. Even if the dollar were to fall on possible BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I think the dollar should firmly be protected around the 132 to 133 yen area," NatWest's Mizukami said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ spent a record $21.35 billion buying yen in April in an effort to bolster the yen, but dealers said they also remember that the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was limited. \par \par \uc2  On April 9 and 10 the BOJ sold dollars in New York and Tokyo, temporarily hammering down the dollar to as low as 127.40 yen. But the dollar has bounced back since then. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ only managed to buy a little time for the yen, the dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The greenback stood at 135.75/80 yen by late Tokyo, compared with 136.22/32 yen in late Monday's New York trade. \par \par \uc2  "Many players are very careful about building dollar longs amid fear over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," NatWest's Mizukami said. \par \par \uc2  "But the dollar is on an upward trend and the market is expected to buy gradually. The market is putting a target for the dollar to go up to about 141 yen within a month or two," he added. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5j04wem\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
