\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr easier vs yen by midday Tokyo, awaits Suharto. \b0\par\par\uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 1998\par 05:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0308 GMT\tab      TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT\par  USD/JPY     135.87/92\tab \tab    136.18-135.63\par  USD/DEM     1.7842/52\tab \tab    1.7858-1.7833\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, May 19 (Reuters) - The dollar was easier versus the \par \par \uc2  yen by midday on Tuesday due to caution over possible Bank of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold \par \par \uc2  dollars to prop up its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  But the yen stayed under pressure on concern over Japan's \par \par \uc2  fragile economy and the Indonesian situation, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  President Suharto's nationwide address has been delayed. \par \par \uc2  Suharto delayed his anxiously awaited address to the nation, originally expected to start at 0200 GMT, because he met community leaders at the presidential palace in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar remains on an uptrend. The sole risk for dollar bulls would be if President Suharto manages to achieve a soft landing in the Indonesian situation," a senior dealer at a Japanese trust bank said. "But that seems highly unlikely under the current scenario." \par \par \uc2  Palace sources said Suharto would answer Monday's call for him to resign by parliament Speaker Harmoko, number three in the ruling structure and an old friend. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah fell to 16,000 to the dollar ahead of key announcements by President Suharto and parliament. Pressured by thousands of students and other demonstrators, members of parliament were due to decide later on Tuesday whether to back their leadership. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah started Singapore trade at around 13,800. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Tuesday, the dollar retreated versus the yen, partly due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of Australia, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The RBA confirmed it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday to buy the Australian dollar against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  This as well as morning remarks by Japan's Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga raised concerns about possible BOJ dollar sales against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Matsunaga said that Japan would act decisively against excessive weakness of the yen. He also said that the yen's excessive weakness is not favourable. \par \par \uc2  "The combination of Matsunaga's remarks and RBA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the day reminded traders of the risk of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer at a European bank. But concern about the Indonesian situation and falling Japanese bond yields and stock prices favoured dollar buying, he said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar briefly rose to 136.18 yen in the morning on purchases by interbank dealers due to expectations of dollar demand related to the setting up of investment trust funds. \par \par \uc2  But buying withered as profit-taking came in, and trade became directionless by late morning, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese bond yields continued falling today. But this was not a fresh factor to make us sell the yen further," said a senior dealer at a long-term credit bank. The dollar jumped to 136.40 yen overnight, its highest since August 1991. \par \par \uc2  The key 182nd 10-year Japanese government bond yield hit yet another record low of 1.240 percent at 0400 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yen would remain on a downtrend. \par \par \uc2  "If there is any bad news related to the banking industry, that could easily result in a dollar rally to 140 yen," said the trust bank dealer. Major Japanese banks are to release their business results for 1997/98 later this week. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Fed policy-makers meet later on Tuesday. Dealers said a rate rise - although the chances are slim of that occurring - would widen the interest rate gap between Japan and the United States, boosting the dollar further against the yen. \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, large-scale student protests are expected on Wednesday. ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3 3432-8570 fax +81-3 3432-7462, tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5j04v2x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
