\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo -2: Japan Stocks Lackluster; JGB Yields Lower \b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 1998\par 03:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar lost a little ground in the wake of yen-supportive comments by Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later rebounded. \par \par \uc2  As reported, Minister of Finance Hikaru Matsunaga warned that Japanese financial authorities would take decisive action to correct the excessively weak yen. Haruhiko Kuroda, head of the ministry's international finance bureau, repeated that warning moments later, adding that investors should be aware of the yen's upside risk. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dipped just below Y135.80 after the comments but quickly recovered the lost ground, amid deep concerns about Japan's economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  Those concerns were underscored by movements in Japan's bond and stock markets. The yield on the benchmark 10-year government bond dipped to yet another record low 1.260%, reflecting notions that deflationary pressure will persist in the economy for now. \par \par \uc2  Also, stock prices remained lackluster. Around 0100 GMT, the Nikkei index was 55.65 points lower at 15,328.82. \par \par \uc2  But traders are still wary about the possibility of yen-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "One scenario is for the BOJ to step in if Suharto announces he will step down, because it's about the only potential yen-bullish factor right now," said ABN-Amro's Takano. \par \par \uc2  But he added \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the current level would only have a limited impact due to a relatively small amount of dollar-long posistions. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  above Y137 would be a lot more effective," he said. \par \par \uc2  The mark is trading at Y76.16, up from Y76.12 earlier but below Y76.30 in New York late Monday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Monday at Y75.70. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6235, unchanged from earlier and above $1.6220 in New York late Monday. Sterling was at $1.6230 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar is seen trading between Y135.50-Y136.40 and\par DEM1.7800-DEM1.7880 for the rest of the Asian day.\par By Sonoko Setaishi 813-5255-2933; ssetaishi@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-05-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0105GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5j047ir\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
