\par\par \b \uc2  Yen mired, dented by mounting Indonesia concern. \b0\par\par\uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 1998\par 09:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 14 (Reuters) - The yen was mired after setting one-month lows against the dollar and 18-month troughs against the mark amid mounting concern about social unrest in Indonesia and the toll it is taking on financial markets in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Lingering wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to hinder attempts the dollar makes to climb above April's 6-1/2-year high of 135.42 yen, but can only temporarily stave off such a move, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The news out of Asia is dreadful and we have yet to see any signs of the yen finding meaningful support," said Kit Juckes, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at NatWest Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  The yen depreciated as far as 134.58 per dollar, its weakest since April 7, and hit 75.62 per mark, its worst showing since November 1996, amid escalating tensions in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  The outbreak of fresh violence in Jakarta on Thursday forced the Indonesia rupiah to two-month lows against the dollar. It weighed on Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and kept the Australian dollar mired near 12-year lows against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not make a lot of sense during the Asian maelstrom," said Juckes at NatWest who sees the dollar rising toward 136 yen in coming days. \par \par \uc2  Japanese economic fundamentals are also weighing on the yen. \par \par \uc2  Thursday's Nihon Keizai Shimbun paper said a senior Bank of Japan official acknowledged deflation could affect the Japanese economy by the end of summer but added that the probability of a deflationary spiral was low, according to Nikkei English news. \par \par \uc2  Japanese economic weakness will undercut the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threats, such as those made on Thursday by Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the Finance Ministry's International Finance Bureau. \par \par \uc2  He said on Thursday that Japan would take appropriate, timely measures in response to the excessive weakness of the yen and that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would eventually affect the market. \par \par \uc2  "Conditions are not right for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and even if there is any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it will only be the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own, and not on a co-ordinated basis," said Brian Martin, chief economist at Barclays Capital in London. \par \par \uc2  He was looking for the dollar to rally to 137.50 yen by the end of next week. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 134.11/21 yen at 0654 GMT from 133.98/03 late in Europe on Wednesday. Mark/yen was at 75.56/59 from 75.34/40 on Wednesday. Dollar/mark was at 1.7748/53 from 1.7770/82 at the close of European trading on Wednesday, undermined by losses in sterling/mark. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was offered short-lived support on Wednesday by the release of stronger-than-expected British economic reports but fell back anew because these were not enough to revive talk of higher interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Sterling/mark weakened to 2.8890/00 by 0813 GMT from 2.9015/25 late in Europe on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark was offered little direction by the Bundesbank policy council meeting on Thursday, with traders expecting the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave its securities repurchase rate unchanged at 3.30 percent. However, a news conference is scheduled at 1200 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank council member Reimut Jochimsen speaks at 1430 GMT. Also on the agenda for Thursday is the release at 1230 GMT of U.S. April consumer prices and real earnings report. ((Swaha Pattanaik, London newsroom, +44 171 542 6284, uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2       Treasuries prices, yields. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5e05eq7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
