\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo -2: Kuroda Comments Pull Down Dlr Slightly \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 1998\par 03:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Underscoring the weak sentiment surrounding Japan's economy Wednesday, Japanese stock prices once again are under pressure. Around 0050 GMT, the Nikkei average was 143.76 points lower from the previous session's close, at 15,178.72. \par \par \uc2  Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials tried to stem the decline of the yen, reiterating a few standard phrases. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the Finance Ministry's international finance bureau, said the yen is excessively weak and Japan will take decisive and appropriate action on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. The dollar fell slightly after the comments were reported, but later bounced back. \par \par \uc2  "With a lack of actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), his words are getting less convincing these days," said a Japanese city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, Vice Minister of Finance for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara said the sharp rise in the country's current account surplus was partly due to the weak yen, and the U.S. understands that. \par \par \uc2  But Sakakibara declined to comment on the dollar-yen, prompting some players to buy the dollar against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Participants will remain on the lookout for yen-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ now that the dollar is hovering above the levels where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last stepped into the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The mark is trading at Y75.42, up from Y75.36 earlier but below Y75.44 in New York late Tuesday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Tuesday at Y74.90. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6330, up from $1.6328 earlier and above $1.6327 in New York late Tuesday. Sterling was at $1.6341 in Tokyo late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar is seen trading between Y134.50-Y133.70 and\par DEM1.7720-DEM1.7790 for the rest of the Asian day.\par By Sonoko Setaishi 813-5255-2933; ssetaishi@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 13-05-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0101GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5d041e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
