\par\par \b \uc2  Yen mired, seen extending slide amid Asian woes. \b0\par\par\uc2 670 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 13 (Reuters) - The yen was mired on Wednesday amid pessimism about Japan's economy and concern about political turbulence in Indonesia, with only the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  protecting it from renewed attack. \par \par \uc2  Traders sold yen for other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as political tensions in Indonesia escalated after six students were killed on Tuesday at an anti-government rally in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Such concern about stability in the region comes at a time when yen bearishness is already being fuelled by the perception that Japan's economy is stagnating and at risk of slipping back into recession, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The economic fundamentals are persuasively in favour of a weaker yen," said Eric Fishwick, international economist at Nikko Europe in London. "The dollar is also very well bid given the bad news coming out of Southeast Asian on an almost daily basis and Japanese banks' exposure to the region." \par \par \uc2  He said he expected dollar/yen to rise beyond the one-month highs already set on Wednesday, and was targeting a move back toward the 6-1/2-year high of 135.42 seen in April. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 134.13/23 yen at 0745 GMT from a session peak of 134.24 and 132.72/82 late in Europe on Tuesday. Mark/yen was at 75.54/58 from 74.65/70 late Tuesday in Europe. \par \par \uc2  Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were dragged lower after the Indonesian rupiah weakened to trade at more than 10,000 per dollar for the first time in more than seven weeks. \par \par \uc2  Pessimism about Japanese domestic demand was reinforced after a report showed Japan's current account surplus rose 43.8 percent in March from a year earlier amid a decline in imports. The surplus in merchandise trade alone rose 38.4 percent from a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials are expected to try to stem yen slippage before leaders of the Group of Seven industrial nations meet this weekend by keeping the fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alive. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, a senior Japanese Finance Ministry official, said on Wednesday the yen had fallen too far against the dollar and that the Finance Ministry would take appropriate action on exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  To be sure, such threats are gradually losing their ability to ward off attack on the yen, especially as traders expect that only the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will conduct such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Ultimately the market is used to the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said James Shugg, economist at Westpac in London. \par \par \uc2  Weakness in the yen and regional Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also took its toll on the Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar fell to fresh 11-1/2-year lows against the dollar, with analysts expecting it to extend its slide. \par \par \uc2  "There are very significant downside risks for the Australian dollar, though not from domestic issues," said Shugg at Westpac. "More bad news out of Asia will drag it even lower." \par \par \uc2  The Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had fallen as low as $0.6291 by 0803 GMT and was at $0.6290/95, about 0.8 percent lower from overnight highs. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark was largely sidelined early in Europe, although news briefings by Bundesbank council members Olaf Sievert and Hans-Juergen Krupp at 0900 GMT could give the mark direction. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was expected to be the main focus in the European morning session with traders eyeing the slew of reports scheduled for release on Wednesday for clues as to whether British interest rates have peaked. \par \par \uc2  April jobless data and March wage costs are out at 0830 GMT, while the Bank of England releases its quarterly inflation report at 0930 GMT and the minutes from the April 9 meeting of its Monetary Policy Committee. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at 2.9001/11 marks at 0808 GMT from 2.8966/71 late in Europe on Tuesday. It was at $1.6323/33 from $1.6295/05 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2    ((Swaha Pattanaik, London newsroom, +44 171 542 6284, \par \par \uc2  uk.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .news@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2       Treasuries prices, yields. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5d05jt5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
