\par\par \b \uc2  INSIGHT - Dlr/yen retains luster, more gains ahead. \b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 1998\par 00:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, May 13 (Reuters) - Dollar/yen retained its luster on Wednesday even as it pared some gains, suggesting the uptrend remained intact, chartists said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen closed the New York day at 134.10/20, below its 134.23/33 opening level but above the key 134 level. \par \par \uc2  "While 134.10 yen is not itself a critical level, it is encouraging that dollar/yen closed above the 134 level," said Pete Grant, senior analyst at Standard & Poor's MMS. \par \par \uc2  Chartists suggested the rally should continue as long as the Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , does not squash the move through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The next resistance level was seen to be near 134.40 yen and after that chartists admitted the dollar could steam ahead briskly before hitting resistance near the 135.40 level. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, slippage below the 134 level toward 133.70 and below could trigger more losses, chartists said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile mark/yen, whose recent strength has surprised some chartists, was "well-contained" on Wednesday. But chartists still expect the pair to move higher in coming sessions, probing 75.70 on the way to the October 1996 high of 75.90. \par \par \uc2  "I have been a bit disappointed by the momentum," Grant said, noting however that this did not signal any reversal. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/mark still appeared range-bound on Wednesday, closing at 1.7784/89, down from the 1.7807/12 opening. \par \par \uc2  While analysts said that they remained "friendly" for dollar/mark, most said resistance at the 1.7800 level would need to be broken more decisively before an attack on the 1.7900 level could be launched. \par \par \uc2  But some analysts said the dollar could hit a wall near the 1.7980 level, unable to vault past the key 1.80 level. \par \par \uc2  For the Australian dollar, which plunged to an 11-1/2 year low under the weight of other beleaguered Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , chartists remained bearish. \par \par \uc2  "I have been bearish for some time and I think the $0.6200 level is well within reach," Grant predicted. \par \par \uc2  The near-term target is $0.6250 analysts said. \par \par \uc2  ((-Svea Herbst-Bayliss, NA Treasury Desk, 212-859-1639 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5d05dos\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
