\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr down after erasing gains on caution before G8. \b0\par\par\uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0615 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     132.54/59\tab \tab 133.22-132.63\par  USD/DEM     1.7665/70\tab \tab 1.7700-1.7640\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, May 11 (Reuters) - The dollar was down against the \par \par \uc2  yen by late afternoon Tokyo on Monday, as earlier buyers of the \par \par \uc2  greenback liquidated longs as caution prevailed ahead of the \par \par \uc2  weekend meeting of the leaders of the Group of Eight nations. \par \par \uc2  Earlier comments by senior Finance Ministry official \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also helped to discourage \par \par \uc2  aggressive dollar buying, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at 132.75/80 yen and 1.7699/04 marks in New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Earlier, some players bought dollars as nothing fresh on dollar/yen came out of the weekend meeting of G7 finance ministers," said a dealer at a trust bank. "But comments by Mr Kuroda were effective in discouraging dollar bulls." \par \par \uc2  Kuroda, director-general of the International Finance Bureau at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF), said on Monday that a statement issued after talks between U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin and Finance Minister Hikaru Matsunaga in London on Friday mentioned joint action in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "The statement said we are prepared to take joint (\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) action," Kuroda told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The statement, issued to reporters by Japanese officials and briefly summing up the content of bilateral talks between Rubin and Matsunaga, said: "They reiterated their commitment to cooperate closely in the exchange markets as appropriate." \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar rose as high as 133.22 yen as interbank players and short-term speculators bought dollars after a communique issued by the G7 finance ministers in London on Saturday made no fresh statement on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The G7 communique welcomed the "substantial" policy measures announced by Japan in April that are aimed at achieving domestic demand-led growth. It also said the G7 looked forward to a successful launch of Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but made no mention of exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was capped by offers from Japanese exporters and profit-taking by U.S. fund operators. Options-linked offers were also lined up around 134 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Earlier dollar buyers turned in sellers after seeing that the upside was heavy around 133.25/35," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  Gains in Tokyo stocks also helped to support the yen, dealers said. The key 225-share Nikkei average closed up 1.54 percent, or 232.90 points, at 15,381.90. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar was underpinned by Japanese investor bids and buying related to the setting up of fresh investment trust funds, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar buying interest is still strong among Japanese investors," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  "But concerns of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) after the Birmingham summit are discouraging aggressive dollar buying." \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said vague talk that the MOF planned to meet officials of Japanese life insurers this week was partly responsible for inviting more dollar selling in late afternoon. \par \par \uc2  But activity was generally slow on Monday, as other financial markets in Asia such as Singapore, Indonesia and Thailand were closed for holidays. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5b05not\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
