\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Mixed; BOJ Stance, U.S. Data Closely Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 1998\par 02:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar edged lower versus the yen in Tokyo trading early Friday compared with its levels late in New York Thursday amid lingering fears that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen and caution ahead of the release of key U.S. economic data. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is slightly higher against the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit an intraday high of $133.48 at the start of Asian trading on buying by Japanese trading houses, but with memories still fresh from the BOJ's huge \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month, the dollar quickly ran into stiff resistance. Last month, the BOJ began selling dollars from around the Y133.60 level. \par \par \uc2  'There is extreme caution around Y133.60,' said Shuji Takano, assistant manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at ABN-Amro Bank N.V. \par \par \uc2  Some are also wary the BOJ - which often times its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to coincide with political events - might step into the market during or after a meeting of finance ministers from the group of seven industrialized nations (G-7), which is scheduled to be held Friday. \par \par \uc2  A senior Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said late Thursday that exchange rates won't be a major topic at the meeting, as ministers are concentrating on issues to be taken up at the G-7 summit to be held in Birmingham later this month. \par \par \uc2  Around 0035 GMT (8:35 p.m. EDT), the dollar was trading at Y133.23, down from Y133.35 around 0001 GMT and below Y133.30 in New York late Thursday. The dollar was quoted at Y133.23 late in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also trading at DEM1.7685, marginally lower than DEM1.7686 earlier and above DEM1.7665 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at DEM1.7657 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 08-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0048GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5803woy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
