\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr off highs at Tokyo noon on caution over BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0300 GMT\tab      TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0300 GMT\par  USD/JPY     133.30/32\tab \tab    133.65-132.94\par  USD/DEM     1.7666/68\tab \tab    1.7673-1.7650\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, May 7 (Reuters) - The dollar was up versus the yen \par \par \uc2  at midday on Thursday but came off earlier highs due to \par \par \uc2  lingering caution over Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      "Considering weakening Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets, \par \par \uc2  including in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reasons for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are in place," \par \par \uc2  said a bank dealer. But whether the BOJ can push the dollar \par \par \uc2  down effectively is another question, he added. \par \par \uc2  In late morning trade, the dollar shot to as high as 133.65 yen due to speculative purchases aimed at triggering stop-loss buying at around 133.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 133.05/15 yen and 1.7637/47 marks in New York on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Sporadic sales by Japanese exporters and profit-taking by some investors kicked in soon after the dollar topped 133.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  "In Tokyo, nobody is willing to keep buying dollars above 133.50 yen because of a possibility of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said the bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Some traders, however, said it may be hard for Japanese monetary authorities to conduct dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a lack of supporting factors. \par \par \uc2  Senior BOJ official Akira Nagashima said on Thursday that the current dollar/yen rate reflected a good U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  This remark was taken by dealers to mean the BOJ may not be much concerned about the dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  BOJ Deputy Governor Yutaka Yamaguchi said a would have merits but also side effects. This raised speculation of a further credit easing in the money market by the BOJ, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The key 182nd cash Japanese bond yield fell to another record low of 1.365 percent as of 0331 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The key 225-share Nikkei average was down 0.56 percent or 85.54 points at 15,158.30 at midday, after rising to 15,244.10 at one point during the morning. \par \par \uc2  "Renewed worries about Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , coupled with weak Japanese stocks and falling Japanese bond yields, won't work in favour of yen buying," said the Japanese bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  In early trade, the Indonesian rupiah fell sharply vs dollar on riots in the north Sumatra city of Medan and several other cities. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah bounced back to around 9100/9300 against the dollar at 0332 GMT after falling to the 10,000 level in early trade. Violence appeared to have subsided in the riot-torn city on Thursday, but the market remained jittery over the situation in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers were concerned about comments on the yuan by an economist at China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Yi Gang, chief economist of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the yuan would remain at current levels against dollar as promised by government. He said in an academic paper given in Australia that pressure would increase in the second half of 1998 for devaluation of the yuan. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong leader Tung Chee-hwa on Thursday reiterated that the. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5705x7f\