\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar maintains firm tone vs yen in nervous Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, May 7 (Reuters) - ASIAN \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ACTIVITY: \par \par \uc2      0022 GMT --*Dollar steady and keeping firm undertone \par \par \uc2  against yen in nervous early Tokyo on Thursday as yen stayed \par \par \uc2  under selling pressure amid worries over Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \par \par \uc2  Japanese share prices, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      *Interbank operators dominated activity in light early \par \par \uc2  trade, with strong bargain-hunting demand protecting dollar's \par \par \uc2  downside below 133.00 yen. \par \par \uc2      *Knockout options rumoured placed at around 133.50 yen and \par \par \uc2  dollar-sales aimed at protecting options may emerge should \par \par \uc2  dollar approach that level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  *Tokyo stocks weaker in early morning trade on concerns over future course of Japanese economy. Market sentiment stayed bearish. At 0031 GMT, Nikkei average down 0.51 percent, or 77.03 points, at 15,166.81. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar stood at 133.05/15 yen and 1.7655/60 marks compared with New York's 133.05/15 and 1.7637/47 respectively. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar carried over bullish trend from overnight against yen, with uptrend in mark/yen giving support to dollar/yen. \par \par \uc2  *But mark capped on slight corrective sales around 75.50 yen in early trade. At 0029 GMT, German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood at 75.37/40 yen, from 75.44 yen in late New York on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  *"With bearish Japanese stocks and concerns over Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  reviving again, the environment around the yen does not look good," a senior city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  *Dealer said fears over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain, but the dollar/yen should be well-supported on dips, with substantial buying demand from Japanese investors. \par \par \uc2  *Finance Ministry announced on Thursday that Japan's customs-cleared trade surplus rose 58.9 percent to 561.24 billion yen in first 20 days of April, compared with revised surplus of 353.18 billion yen in same period last year, but market shrugged off results. \par \par \uc2  *Selling interest from Japanese exporters expected above 133.50 yen, which should make operators cautious about testing above that level, but growing worries about Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to riots in Indonesia may hurt undertone of yen. \par \par \uc2  *Market operators to closely watch situation in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets. \par \par \uc2  *At 0044 GMT, Indonesia rupiah at 9,500/10,000 against dollar, from 8,350/8,430 in late Asian trade on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  *Some dealers concerned about comments on yuan by chief economist of China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers said they want to see how comments will affect Hong Kong dollar. \par \par \uc2  *Yi Gang, chief economist of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said yuan will remain at current level against dollar as promised by government. But he said in an academic paper given in Australia that pressure would increase in second half of 1998 for devaluation of yuan. \par \par \uc2  2300 GMT \par \par \uc2  *Dollar softer vs yen in early Asia on Thursday due to light profit-taking following overnight rallies. \par \par \uc2  *Corrective sales in mark/yen also factor weighing down dollar/yen. Dollar firmed against mark. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar sentiment stayed bullish, but concern over possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to intensify should dollar approach 133.50/60 yen - level where BOJ sold dollars in New York early in April. \par \par \uc2  *Mark edged lower in early trade on corrective sales following decisive break above 75.00 yen overnight. Dealers expect mark to test next target of 75.90 yen. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5705ww4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
