\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr higher after fall in Tokyo stocks, JGB yields. \b0\par\par\uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab  0615 GMT\tab     TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT\par  USD/JPY     133.25/30\tab \tab 133.65-132.94\par  USD/DEM     1.7667/70\tab \tab 1.7673-1.7650\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2      TOKYO, May 7 (Reuters) - The dollar was higher against the \par \par \uc2  yen by late afternoon in Tokyo on Thursday, but its upside was \par \par \uc2  capped by concerns over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Falling Tokyo share prices and Japanese government bond \par \par \uc2  (JGB) yields, and weakness in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed on \par \par \uc2  the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The greenback rose to the day's high of 133.65 yen in late morning trade on speculative purchases aimed at triggering stop-loss buy orders around 133.50 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Comments by senior BOJ official Akira Nagashima that the current dollar/yen rate reflected sound economic fundamentals in the United States also briefly fueled dollar buying, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. economy is doing well and the current \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates reflect such U.S. fundamentals," Nagashima, the BOJ's executive director, was quoted by a BOJ spokesman as telling parliamentary officials who visited the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Stop-losses were triggered around 133.50 yen, but the dollar was capped by profit-taking by interbank players and selling by Japanese exporters and trust banks," said a dealer at a long-term credit bank. \par \par \uc2  "People were reluctant to continue buying dollars due possible BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Renewed weakness in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also a factor that weighed on the yen in the morning. \par \par \uc2  But pressure on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased as some Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  pared losses in the afternoon, a dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah bounced back to around 9,310/9,410 to the dollar by 0630 GMT after falling to around 9,700/10,200 earlier. The rupiah closed at 8,700 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Violence appeared to have subsided in the North Sumatra city of Medan on Thursday, but the market remained jittery over the situation in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  "Pressure on the yen eased a bit in the afternoon as the rupiah did not continue to weaken beyond 10,000," the European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "But the yen's recovery was limited as Tokyo stocks and JGB yields remained down." \par \par \uc2  The key 225-share Nikkei average ended down 0.66 percent, or 100.81 points, at 15,143.03, after falling as low as 15,020.05. \par \par \uc2  The yield of the benchmark 182nd 10-year JGB fell to a record low of 1.350 percent, from Wednesday's close of 1.400 percent. \par \par \uc2  But the market was still cautious about buying dollars too aggressively ahead of a meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors of the Group of Seven (G7) industrialised nations on Friday and Saturday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Comments by U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin on Wednesday that the G7 nations would discuss exchange rates and he expects "some discussion" of the euro, made the market cautious about actively bidding up dollar/yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There's always a discussion of exchange rate and things of that matter," Rubin said. He was speaking on the eve of his departure to London, where the ministers will gather on Friday and Saturday to prepare for a summit of leaders from the G8 in Birmingham the following weekend. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 133.05/15 yen and 1.7637/47 marks in New York on Wednesday. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5705wkf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
