t the current level of 8.27 yuan/$ as promised repeatedly by the government, but pressure for devaluation will increase in the second half of 1998 due to the impact of the financial crisis on China's exports," Yi said. The paper, presented jointly with Song Li-Gang of the Australian National University earlier this week, was reproduced in full on the website of the Australian Financial Review newpaper. \par \par \uc2  *Dollar expected to be supported on bargain-hunting demand by Japanese investors. \par \par \uc2  *Firm technical support seen around 132.50/60 yen. \par \par \uc2  *Mark edged lower in early trade on corrective sales following decisive break above 75.00 yen overnight. Dealers expect mark to test next target of 75.90 yen. \par \par \uc2  *As of 2338 GMT, mark stood at 75.30/33 yen compared with 75.44 yen in late New York on Wednesday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5605w7p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
