\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup -2: ECB President Choice Key For Markets \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Mai 1998\par 08:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that most market participants were wary of carrying big positions over Japan's long weekend, especially with the specter of possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hanging in the air. The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  April 9 when the dollar was trading around Y133.20-Y133.30. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns and profit-taking interest likely will cap the dollar's upside at Y133.25 for now, with further resistance pegged at Y133.50, traders said. \par \par \uc2  In addition to the holidays, caution ahead of this weekend's summit of European Union leaders discouraged aggressive trading Friday, participants said. \par \par \uc2  'It's really difficult to take positions ahead of the long weekend (in both Europe and Japan),' said a trader at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  'The summit over the weekend could move the markets, but most of the points of the EMU are set,' he said, adding that markets will focus on the dispute over who will become the first governor of the European community's new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Leaders from the E.U meeting this weekend in Brussels are set to confirm the 11 countries that will be joining the first wave of European Monetary Union on Jan 1., 1998, and set parity exchange rates for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro. \par \par \uc2  'The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head is the real question' that markets are interested in, said Callum Henderson, managing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at S&P/MMS in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  He said that if Wim Duisenberg, current president of the European Monetary Institute, were selected for a full eight-year term it would be very positive for the mark because it would 'point to credibility for the euro.' \par \par \uc2  But no agreement on the central banker this weekend or a decision to create a shared term would be negative for the mark, he said. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6730, up from $1.6708 in New York late Thursday. Sterling was at $1.6725 in London late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0615GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5103ohb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
