\par\par \b \uc2  Yen Cross-European units firm in pre-holiday Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2 449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 1 (Reuters) - European units posted healthy gains versus the yen in late yen-cross trade on Friday in tandem with the dollar's rise against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Trade was subdued due to the May Day holiday on Friday in Europe and other Asian markets and ahead of a four-day weekend in Tokyo for the Golden Week holidays. \par \par \uc2  "The German mark rose partly because it is easy to buy up the mark/yen than the dollar/yen. The rate is free from concerns of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ)," said a senior dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar briefly rose to 133.19 yen on Friday midday, its highest level since the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  via the New York Federal Reserve Bank to sell dollars in New York on April 9. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 132.93/98 yen at 0531 GMT against 132.80/90 yen in late New York on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The German mark was at 74.16/19 yen after light stop-loss sell orders were triggered above 74 yen. It was around 73.98 yen in late New York on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But scattered selling by Japanese exporters kept the mark from rising further, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Profit-taking was also detected ahead of a three-day European Union summit starting later on Friday that is to decide which countries join the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said focus will be who is the future head of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) and whether it is decided during the summit. Some said the decision could be postponed. \par \par \uc2  "The most bullish scenario for European units will be that Duisenberg is chosen as ECB head this weekend, and there is no further dispute over the top post," said the senior dealer. \par \par \uc2  "But if not, European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be sold, depending on how far off this scenario is," he said. \par \par \uc2  A majority of EU members have said they were prepared to back Netherland's Wim Duisenberg, head of the ECB forerunner, the European Monetary Institute, as the first ECB president. \par \par \uc2  But France has throw a spanner in the works by putting up Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet as a candidate, setting off a row that threatens to spoil the EU summit. \par \par \uc2  The British pound was at 222.43/55 yen at 0541 GMT, against around 222.11 yen in late New York on Thursday, while the Swiss franc was at 88.69/74 yen versus around 88.47 yen in New York. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3 3432-8570 fax +81-3 3432-7462, tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5106ba8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
