\par\par \b \uc2  Japan's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  backs yen with record $21 billion - bankers. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 497 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Mai 1998\par 16:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record $21.4 billion buying yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in April in a bid to bolster the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the effort was mixed at best, bankers said Friday. \par \par \uc2  They said the scale of the Bank of Japan's April dollar-sales had tripled from December, when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars and buy yen for the first time in more than five years. \par \par \uc2  "Considering the amount that the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through our bank, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (in April) was the largest in my memory," a senior banker said. \par \par \uc2  The banker said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted its largest yearly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1996, when it bought about $55 billion with yen in a bid to halt the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Now the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling dollars and buying yen in a bid to prop up the weak Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has fueled a rise in exports and swelled Japan's trade surplus with the United States, sparking concern among American manufacturers, especially automakers. \par \par \uc2  Traders had not initially realized the scale of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early April, as its impact on dollar-yen trading was limited and the dollar kept rising, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  A cheap yen makes Japanese exports less costly and more competitive on world markets. \par \par \uc2  One banker said the actual amount of April dollar-sales by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been larger than the $21.4 billion estimated by most bankers, since additional funds may have been used. \par \par \uc2  Analysts and bankers estimated the amount of dollar selling and yen buying from Finance Ministry data released Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry has confirmed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell dollars on April 9 in New York. Bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was detected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in Tokyo the following day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar moved in a range of 127.40 yen to 133.50 yen in trading in New York and Tokyo on those days. The dollar stood at 133 yen late in Tokyo Friday and at 133.30 early in New York. \par \par \uc2  "There were mixed views among market participants (after the April \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," another senior banker said. \par \par \uc2  "Some said it was big and others said it was not. That says the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not have worked effectively, despite the large scale of the action." \par \par \uc2  The banker said the cost effectiveness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared poor and that there was talk it had caused problems for the Federal Reserve, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had to absorb funds after it was flooded with dollars. \par \par \uc2  "I've heard the United States may not be too happy about the consequences, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caused some confusion in U.S. markets," the banker said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also caused an unexpected rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key short-term interest rates in mid-April. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du51066yd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
