\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ backs yen with record $21 billion - bankers. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 625 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Mai 1998\par 11:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 1 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan (BOJ) spent a record $21.35 billion buying yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in April as part of its efforts to bolster the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bankers said on Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data released on Friday showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  received 2.7752 trillion yen - $21.35 billion at 130 yen to the dollar - from the private sector in April through its special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the volume of dollar-sales \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in yen terms could be roughly estimated from the Finance Ministry data - which is taken to include receipts from such entities as commercial banks, foreign central banks, municipal governments, public funds and quasi-government institutions - minus the ministry's sales of financing bills (FBs). \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry sold no FBs to the private sector in April. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the scale of the Bank of Japan's April dollar-sales had tripled compared with December, when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars for the first time in more than five years. \par \par \uc2  In December, Japan's foreign reserves declined $7.593 billion to $220.792 billion. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry announced on Friday that the external reserves had dropped a record $17.835 billion in April to $205.758 billion. The reserves stood at $223.593 billion in March. \par \par \uc2  The previous record decline was seen in March 1991, when the reserves dropped by $8.08 billion. \par \par \uc2  "Considering the amount that the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through our bank, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (in April) was the largest in my memory," a senior banker said. \par \par \uc2  The banker said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted its largest yearly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1996, when it bought about $55 billion with yen to halt the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  The banker said the actual amount of April dollar-sales could be larger than the $21.35 billion estimated by most bankers, since funds from MOF deposits at commercial banks had also been used. \par \par \uc2  The market had not at first realised the scale of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early April, as its impact on dollar/yen trade was limited and the U.S. unit remained bullish, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry has confirmed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell dollars on April 9 in New York. Bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was detected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in Tokyo the following day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar moved in a range of 127.40 yen to 133.50 yen during those days in New York and Tokyo trade. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 133.00/05 yen in late afternoon trade on Friday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "There were mixed views among market participants (after the April \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). Some said it was big and others said it was not," another senior banker said. "That says the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not have worked effectively, despite the large scale of the action." \par \par \uc2  The banker said the cost effectiveness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared poor and that there was talk it had caused problems for the U.S. Federal Reserve, which had had to absorb funds in the money market after it was flooded by dollars. \par \par \uc2  "I've heard the United States may not be too happy about the consequences, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caused some confusion in U.S. markets," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also caused an unexpected rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key short-term rates in mid-April. \par \par \uc2  Traders said settlement of the Bank of Japan's dollar-sales triggered a rise in the key unsecured overnight call rate that was exacerbated by confusion over the exact settlement time for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du51063do\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
