\par\par \b \uc2  Japan April external reserves post record drop-MOF. \b0\par\par\uc2 199 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Mai 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 1 (Reuters) - Japan's external reserves posted their steepest monthly drop ever in April, an official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  MOF announced on Friday that external reserves fell $17.835 billion from a month earlier to $205.758 billion at the end of April. \par \par \uc2  The previous record monthly decline in external reserves was a drop of $8.08 billion posted in March 1991. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) was the chief cause of the sharp drop in external reserves, the MOF official told reporters. \par \par \uc2  In addition to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , various other factors affected \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's external reserves, the MOF official said. \par \par \uc2  In April, reevaluation of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings made a positive contribution to external reserves, he said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars in New York on April 9 and in Tokyo on April 10, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the BOJ may have also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  quietly on other days in April. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on April 9 was confirmed by MOF. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 \par \par \uc2  tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du510637q\par }